hysical exercise on to the  brain and it appears to be linked to  mechanisms of plasticity in that lisa's  as one can prove them in humans with  brain imaging and brain stimulation  techniques but but i think rather than  getting at the level of suggestions you  should sleep better you know avoid  medications that are bad for you eat the  right thing and the right amount and you  know exercise and challenge your brain  with new things and have social  relationships all those things are true  and but but we should be able to get to  enough understanding that we can  prescribe it that we can tell then this  is the number of hours of this exercise  that you need to do and here's how we're  going to help you actually convert this  this hopes into realities right because  it's hard to stick with a program like  that so I think that stay that's the  step that we still don't have is the  understanding of how to actually make  this a prescribed herbal intervention  like we do with medications we don't  tell patients take something for that  you know  we tell them what to take and  mods and so forth and so I think we need  that level of understanding but what  about new happiness set points right  everybody wants wellness everybody so is  it possible that we're gonna someday  understand the brain well enough to say  oK you've been through a really terrible  life trauma but we can actually help  your set point well I think you know I  would think about sort of maybe not  happiness but that feeling of being able  to regulate your emotions to be able to  feel less sad when you want to be able  to feel more sad when you want to kind  of have that emotion regulation ability  and so there are studies for example  with people who meditate which we  generally think of as a healthy  lifestyle practice but there are  different levels of expertise and  meditation right so there are Buddhist  monks who do this for say 40,000 hours  in total versus really really dedicated  meditators who